      quartile with a line at the median. Quartiles are R's default "type 7" sample quantiles.
      Whiskers reach the most extreme values within 1.5 IQR of the box (Tukey's rule), and values
      beyond are drawn as outlier points. R's [boxplot()] instead uses Tukey's hinges
      ([fivenum()]), so for some sample sizes the box edges and the fences differ slightly from R:
      for 1, ..., 9, 40 this gives quartiles 3.25 and 7.75 where R draws hinges at 3 and 8. All
      boxes share [color]; the title and axis labels keep their defaults.

