(** B-spline design factory, analogous to R's splines::bs(). Owns a clamped basis on fixed
    boundaries, reused for training and prediction. By default the first basis column is
    omitted, so a formula's intercept does not duplicate the partition of unity. No fitting or
    smoothing is performed. Const evaluations are independent and safe to run concurrently.

    {b Example:}

    {@cpp[
    const dm::Bspline basis(0, 1, {0, 0.5, 1});
    const auto design = basis.eval({0, 0.5, 1});
    std::print("{} {}\n", design.rows(), design.cols()); // 3 4
    ]}

    {b References:}

    {ul
    {- C. de Boor (1972). "On calculating with B-splines". Journal of Approximation Theory 6(1), 50-62. doi:10.1016/0021-9045(72)90080-9.}}

    C++ class [datamunge::Bspline].

    @see "bs()" C++ [bs()]
    @see "fda::BSplineBasis" C++ [fda::BSplineBasis]
    @see "stats::LM" C++ [stats::LM] *)
