    coefficients (d = 2 by default). Uniform knots continue past both ends of the data without
    repeated boundary knots. When d <= degree+1, polynomials of degree < d go unpenalized: λ
    → ∞ gives the least-squares line for d = 2. A rich basis can include functions with no
    data under them if the data identify the penalty nullspace. Without an explicit λ, it is
