(** [n] colours from dark blue through white to dark red, a diverging palette for signed values
    such as correlations (ColorBrewer's RdBu, reversed so that low is blue).

    Interpolates linearly between the seven RdBu anchor colours; an odd [n] puts pure near-white
    (247, 247, 247) in the middle, so with [z_min = -z_max] in RPlot::image() zero maps to
    white.

    {b Example:}

    {@cpp[
    const auto pal = dm::graphics::diverging_colors(3);
    std::print("{} {} {}\n", pal[0].r, pal[1].g, pal[2].r);  // 33 247 178
    ]}

    {b References:}

    {ul
    {- C. Brewer, ColorBrewer 2.0 (RdBu scheme): https://colorbrewer2.org}}

    C++: [std::vector<RGBA> datamunge::graphics::diverging_colors(std::size_t n)]

    @param n Number of colours (at least 1; 1 gives the white midpoint).
    @return The palette, low (blue) to high (red).
    @raise Invalid_argument If [n] is 0. (C++ [std::invalid_argument])
    @see "terrain_colors()" C++ [terrain_colors()]
    @see "RPlot::image()" C++ [RPlot::image()] *)
