    @param a Nonempty finite scalar sequence, length at most INT_MAX.
    @param b Nonempty finite scalar sequence, length at most INT_MAX.
    @return Independent optimal result and counts, with no retained input/cost history.
    @raise Invalid_argument For empty or nonfinite input. (C++ [std::invalid_argument])
    @raise Error [(`Length_error, _)] For geometry/index/container bounds. (C++
      [std::length_error])
    @raise Error [(`Arithmetic, _)] If the final minimum is not finite double. (C++
      [std::overflow_error])
    @raise Out_of_memory If scratch or result storage cannot be allocated. (C++
      [std::bad_alloc])
